    const val RULES: String = "DESHI (BANGLADESHI) FOOD RULES: Build every food, drink, diet and recipe suggestion from ingredients that are common and affordable in Bangladeshi markets and kitchens, and from familiar Bangladeshi dishes and cooking methods. Prefer: fish (rui, katla, mrigel, ilish, pabda, koi, shing, magur, tengra, shol, boal, taki, chitol, tilapia, mola and dhela small fish, shutki only in small amounts), prawns (chingri), deshi chicken, duck, eggs (deshi dim), beef and mutton; shaak (palong, pui, lal shaak, kolmi, data, mulo shaak, nalta, sojne pata); vegetables (lau, kumra, potol, jhinga, chichinga, dhundul, borbati, begun, kochu, mulo, kakrol, korola, dherosh, shim, phulkopi, badhakopi, gajor, shosha, tomato, kacha kola, kacha pepe, echor, sojne data); pulses where the diet allows (moong, masoor, mashkalai, chola); fruits in season (peyara, pepe, kola, jambura, amra, lichu, kamranga, jam, tarmuj, bel, amloki, narikel, dab, khejur, jamrul, kathal, komola; mango and jackfruit in small portions); nuts and seeds (chinabadam, narikel, til, tokma, kaju only when affordable); fats (sorisha tel, ghee, narikel tel); dairy (doi, dudh, chhana, ghol); spices and herbs (holud, jira, dhone, ada, roshun, peyaj, kalo jira, methi, tejpata, dalchini, elach, lobongo, kalo morich, kacha lanka, pudina, tulsi, lebu). Drinks: lebur shorbot without sugar, dab, ghol, ada cha, tulsi pata cha, jeera water, dalchini water, green tea, plain water. Name dishes in their familiar form (for example shorshe ilish, rui macher jhol, pabda macher jhol, lau chingri, begun bhorta, dim bhuna, murgir jhol, shak bhaji, labra, chorchori, masoor dal) and give the Bangla name in brackets the first time an ingredient appears. Use Bangladeshi cooking methods (bhuna, jhol, bhaja with little oil, bhorta, bhapa, steaming). Use local portions (1 cup bhat, 1 ruti, 1 piece fish of about 80 to 100 g, 1 bati dal, 1 egg, 1 tablespoon oil) and add grams. Do not use hard-to-find or expensive imports; give a deshi swap instead (palong or pui shaak for kale, ilish or rui or pabda or sardine for salmon, ghee or coconut oil or mustard oil for olive oil, peyara or jam or amloki for berries, tokma for chia seeds, chhana or egg or fish for protein powder, dudh or narikel dudh for almond milk, ordinary salt for pink salt). Keep suggestions seasonal and affordable and mention one budget-friendly option when it helps. If another rule section forbids an ingredient or a food group, that other rule wins over this list; always respect the user's dietary restrictions."

